mtplx ignore-eos patch (for the serve-bench.py --vs mtplx arm)

Adds an MTPLX_IGNORE_EOS environment switch to the default stop tokens of
mtplx. When it is "1", a reply stops only at max_tokens, so serve-bench.py
measures decode over the same fixed token window as on the gmlx and
llama-server arms, which run with --ignore-eos. serve-bench.py sets the switch
on the mtplx server and refuses an mtplx without the patch.

MTPLX is Apache-2.0, Copyright 2026 Youssof Altoukhi
(https://github.com/youssofal/mtplx). This patch changes mtplx/generation.py.

Baseline: mtplx 2.12.2. Apply it to the mtplx installed in its venv:
  site=$(~/.venvs/mtplx/bin/python -c 'import sysconfig; print(sysconfig.get_paths()["purelib"])')
  patch -p1 -d "$site" < /path/to/bench/patches/mtplx-ignore-eos.patch

--- a/mtplx/generation.py	2026-10-13 10:39:43
+++ b/mtplx/generation.py	2026-10-13 10:39:43
@@ -7280,6 +7280,8 @@
 
 def _default_stop_tokens(tokenizer) -> set[int]:
     ids: set[int] = set()
+    if os.environ.get("MTPLX_IGNORE_EOS") == "1":
+        return ids
     for attr in ("eos_token_id", "pad_token_id"):
         value = getattr(tokenizer, attr, None)
